            "embedding_text": "Authority: Merchant_Fraud\n\n        Document: jrfm-18-00130\n\n        Chapter:\n        \n        \n\n        Section:\n        \n\n        Heading:\n        \n\n        Content:\n\n        The paper presents a comprehensive analysis of using machine learning (ML) for fraud detection in the banking sector, focusing on synthetic data generation, algorithmic approaches (e.g., XGBoost), and evaluation of detection systems. Fraud is framed as a binary classification problem, distinguishing between normal and fraudulent transactions, with a strong emphasis on feature engineering and temporal analysis."
